{% comment %}
  ELSORA DESIGN TOKENS — single source of truth for the 9 ELSORA product-page
  sections, the elsora-wave-divider component, the shared footer gradient,
  and (on the PDRN sandbox only) the header cart-icon tint.

  Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid, which passes an `active_palette`
  parameter that is 'current' for every page EXCEPT the PDRN sandbox
  template, which requests 'ice-globes' for itself.

  FINAL REFERENCE-MATCH CORRECTION: rebuilt from the Chief of Operations'
  exact reference family (soft silver #F3F6F6, cool light grey #DDE8E8,
  very light aqua #D8F0F1, soft aqua #BFE5E8, premium turquoise #35B9C5,
  stronger turquoise #20AEBB, deep accent #168F9B used sparingly, near-
  white #FAFCFC). Explicitly moving away from the greener/darker teal
  values used in prior passes (#159B96, #008F9A, #005A63) per direct
  feedback that those read as "medical/petroleum teal" rather than true
  aqua-leaning turquoise.

  WAVE-ONLY TOKENS (ice_wave_1/2/3 below): dedicated color slots used
  exclusively by sections/elsora-wave-divider.liquid's three fill layers.
  Kept deliberately separate from --elsora-cream-deep/--elsora-tint/
  --elsora-rose (which are shared by the hero background, shipping cards,
  etc.) specifically so a wave-only color correction never ripples into
  those other components. ice_wave_1 (lowest/base layer) is now a clearly
  saturated icy blue — intentionally DIFFERENT from ice_cta (the CTA
  button's own dedicated token, still #706FCB) per explicit instruction
  that the wave base must read as blue, not purple, while every other
  purple usage on the page (CTA, eyebrows, section labels, benefit-card
  icons/headings, review avatars/stars) stays untouched.

  TYPOGRAPHY: --elsora-font-display and --elsora-font-body both use the
  system stack "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif (no web font is
  loaded; this matches the approved theme-editor look). Jost was removed. Normal-cut headings/body/UI text
  must stay within 300/400/500 — those are the only cuts most components
  are styled for. A single explicit exception: weight 200 is also used
  (normal style only) for the hero price row ($ symbol, current price,
  struck-through compare price in sections/hero-banner.liquid) per direct
  instruction to push that one element as thin/premium as possible beyond
  what 300 gave visually. Do not spread weight 200 to any other component
  without a similar explicit request.

  ICE-GLOBES TEXT COLOR (premium black pass): ice_plum changed from the
  near-black navy #172333 to a true rich black #0D0D0D per explicit
  instruction that all black/near-black text (headings + body) read as
  a deliberate premium black rather than a tinted navy. ice_plum_soft
  (secondary/description gray) and ice_label_ink (badge text) were left
  untouched — neither qualifies as "black or near-black", and badges were
  explicitly excluded from the color pass.

  HEADING SHADOW (sandbox only): --elsora-text-shadow-3d (headings) and
  --elsora-text-shadow-3d-sm (hero price) are plain, soft dark drop shadows
  (no light highlight / emboss edge, darkness kept light on purpose — the
  saturated pure black is reserved for the announcement bar only).
  --elsora-text-shadow-3d-footer is a slightly stronger version used ONLY
  for the footer newsletter heading (it sits on the darker teal footer
  gradient where the normal shadow is barely visible). They are applied by
  the ice-globes-only rule block at the bottom of this snippet, to the hero
  title + price, the five section headings (not the final CTA) and the
  footer newsletter heading.
{% endcomment %}

